# Copy to .env (optional). Root .gitignore ignores .env — do not commit secrets.

# --- Local testing (default)
# If you open the app at http://localhost:5173 or http://127.0.0.1:5173, src/config/api.ts
# normally uses http://127.0.0.1:5001 unless VITE_API_URL is set.
#
# Cashfree prod keys locally: HTTPS return URL is required — use `npm run dev:https` instead of `npm run dev`
# (see docs/local-cashfree-testing.md). Comment out VITE_API_URL in .env.development.local for that mode;
# the script enables VITE_API_RELATIVE which proxies `/api` to Flask (same origin, no mixed content).
#
# Overrides:
# VITE_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5001
#
# If you open the dev server by machine IP (e.g. phone on same Wi‑Fi), point the SPA at your PC API, e.g.:
# VITE_API_URL=http://192.168.x.x:5001
# (Without this, non-localhost hosts default to the deployed API — correct for Vercel/production.)
#
# Course cover uploads: if the admin UI hits local API but the public site uses the
# deployed API, configure backend/.env with COURSE_MEDIA_S3_BUCKET (dev bucket) so uploads
# land in S3 — otherwise covers exist only on your laptop and the live site shows broken images.

# --- Production / staging (Amplify or CI)
# Set VITE_API_URL in the hosting provider’s environment before build, e.g.:
# VITE_API_URL=https://YOUR_API_ID.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/dev
#
# Must match backend ADMIN_PANEL_ALLOWED_EMAIL (admin route guards + admin login UI).
# VITE_ADMIN_PANEL_ALLOWED_EMAIL=admin@xpertintern.com

# --- Strapi blog (blog-cms)
# Local: start Strapi in blog-cms (npm run develop, default http://localhost:1337)
# VITE_STRAPI_URL=http://localhost:1337
# Vercel / production: in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables (Production + Preview):
# VITE_STRAPI_URL=https://your-strapi.onrender.com
# No trailing slash. Redeploy after changing (Vite bakes this in at build time).
# On Render (Strapi), set CORS_ORIGIN to your Vercel URL(s), comma-separated, e.g.:
# CORS_ORIGIN=https://your-app.vercel.app
